ap composition silently discards conflicting protection requirements. release_hashes overwrites release-manifest entries with integrity-inventory entries; protected_hashes can overwrite earlier expected hashes with current filesystem hashes; check_protection merges controls over protected hashes. If overlapping entries disagree, only the last expectation is checked, so a protection check can pass despite violating an earlier frozen expectation. Repair: merge through a helper that permits duplicate paths only when expected hashes agree, rejects conflicts before execution, and never replaces an authoritative expected hash with a freshly observed hash.\",\n    \"Legacy-check failure logs are lost on the repair path. baseline captures stdout in StringIO but writes the log only after runpy.run_path returns normally. If a check raises or exits unsuccessfully, the captured diagnostic output disappears; stderr is not included either. This removes evidence needed to explain the failure and inform repair and subsequent review. Repair: persist captured output in a finally block, capture stderr as well, record the failure outcome, and propagate the original failure without converting it into acceptance.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_actions\": [\n    \"Implement atomic, verified preservation with recovery for interrupted copies.\",\n    \"Reject inconsistent overlapping protection hashes instead of silently overwriting them.\",\n    \"Persist legacy-check diagnostics on both success and failure.\",\n    \"Add focused regression coverage for these failure paths, rerun controller verification, and obtain fresh read-only review.\"\n  ],\n  \"residuals\": [\n    \"source_register checks counts against two fields from coverage.json, not independently against the accepted 192-report panel. Its correctness therefore requires an upstream frozen-input check that guarantees the accepted panel and cannot be bypassed; that call-order guarantee is not supplied.\",\n    \"Controller-test cache reuse assumes unchanged control hashes are sufficient despite possible environment changes and does not check that the referenced log still exists. The intended cache-validity and log-retention guarantees are not supplied.\",\n    \"editable_files inventories selected directories and suffixes, rather than all tracked files. The stated guarantee that deleted tracked files fail requires either a narrower explicit meaning of 'tracked' or an additional deletion check outside this excerpt.\",\n    \"Process bounds, exclusive locking, approval-rule behavior and full phase transitions cannot be independently verified from the supplied excerpts. Their stated interfaces are accepted for this bounded review.\",\n    \"Source checks and scoped internal acceptance do not close accounting, scientific or human-acceptance gaps.\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [],\n  \"summary\": \"Revise preservation recovery, conflicting protection-hash handling and failure-log retention. These defects affect resumability and durable evidence under ordinary failures.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"REVISE\"\n}"}}
